course: dictionary
lesson: 15718
title: Traction: the grip that keeps you moving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Traction is a noun, and it mostly means grip. It is the force that stops a wheel, shoe or tyre from slipping on a surface. «The runners wore spiky shoes for better traction on the muddy track.» The shoes did not slip, because they gripped the mud.
explain: Traction can also mean a pulling force. «The engine provided the traction to pull the long train.» Here nothing is gripping. The engine is pulling the train along. Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence, and the meaning will be clear.
explain: Traction has other meanings too. «The doctor put Sam's leg in traction, with weights and pulleys, to help the broken bone heal straight.» In hospital, traction means gentle, steady pulling. Informally, «The idea gained traction when more people in the class supported it» means the idea got more and more support.
fact: Traction is a noun. It is usually uncountable, so we say «good traction», not «a traction».
fact: «Traction» means grip, the force that stops slipping, or the pulling force that moves something along.
fact: Friction helps traction: rough surfaces give more traction, while ice and wet leaves give less.
fact: In hospital, «traction» means gentle, steady pulling with weights and pulleys, to bring a bone or back into the right place.
fact: «Gain traction» means an idea or plan gets more and more support. «Lose traction» means a wheel or shoe starts to slip.
exercise: «The runners wore spiky shoes for better traction on the muddy track.» What does traction mean here? | A kind of cold drink | Time spent warming up | *Grip that stops slipping | A loud noise made by the shoes
exercise: «Ice and wet leaves give very little traction, so cars skid easily.» What makes a car skid easily? | Rough gravel | *Ice | Dry concrete | Rubber mats
exercise: «The idea gained traction when more people in the class supported it.» What does gained traction mean? | *Got more and more support | Became heavier | Was forgotten | Was written down twice
test: «Mia's broken arm was put in traction so the bone could heal straight.» What is traction in this sentence? | A type of bandage | *Gentle, steady pulling with weights and pulleys | Loud noise from the hospital | A kind of sling for the arm
test: «The engine provided the traction to pull the long train.» What does traction mean here? | Paint for the carriages | *A pulling force that moves something along | A whistle sound | A kind of brake
exam: What does «the car lost traction on the ice» mean? | The car stopped to have a rest | *The tyres slipped and did not grip | The car became lighter and floated | The tyres gripped the ice very tightly
